---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<PageLayout
  title="How We Write and Check Our Pages"
  seoTitle="Editorial Policy"
  description="How Golden Moments researches, writes, sources and updates its dementia activity and brain health pages, and what we will never publish."
  path="/editorial-policy/"
  crumb="Editorial policy"
  updated="2026-10-25"
>
  <h2>Our sources</h2>
  <p>
    We base our guides on public guidance from organizations such as the National Institute on Aging, the CDC, the
    Alzheimer’s Association, the Alzheimer’s Foundation of America, the Family Caregiver Alliance and the NHS, and on
    peer-reviewed research such as Cochrane reviews and large clinical trials. Every guide lists the sources it relies
    on. We open each source before citing it, and we only report what it actually says.
  </p>
  <h2>How we write</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Practical first: what to do today, in plain language.</li>
    <li>Honest about evidence: we say “linked with”, “may” and “the evidence is mixed” when that is the truth.</li>
    <li>Respectful: we write about people living with dementia as adults, and we never use quizzing or shaming language.</li>
    <li>No invented content: no made-up statistics, quotes, experts, studies, reviews or testimonials.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who reviews our pages</h2>
  <p>
    Pages are written and checked by the Golden Moments team, with help from AI writing tools for research and drafting.
    Every page is checked against its sources by the team. Our pages have <strong>not</strong> been reviewed by a doctor or
    other clinician, and we do not claim otherwise. They are general information, not medical advice.
  </p>
  <h2>What we will never publish</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Claims that a game, food, supplement, fast or routine prevents, treats, slows or cures dementia.</li>
    <li>Tests, quizzes or scores that suggest someone has, or does not have, dementia.</li>
    <li>Advice to start, stop or change any medicine.</li>
    <li>Advertising or sponsored content disguised as guidance.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Each page shows the date it was last updated. If you find a mistake or an out-of-date source, please email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a> and we will check it promptly.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
